---
title: Voice line - barge-in without dropped or duplicated turns
---
sequenceDiagram
    actor U as Caller
    participant P as Playback
    participant VAD as WebRTC + Silero VAD
    participant C as Turn coordinator
    participant STT as Groq Whisper
    participant S as SupportService + local TTS

    C->>P: start_playback(turn 1)
    U->>VAD: Short noise burst
    VAD-->>C: WebRTC candidate rejected by Silero
    Note over P,C: No interruption, playback continues
    U->>VAD: "Wait, wrong order"
    VAD->>C: Speech confirmed
    C->>P: cancel() about 114-127 ms after confirmation
    Note over C: Start turn 2, turn 1 becomes stale
    VAD->>C: End of speech
    C->>STT: Transcribe (one retry on failure)
    alt STT fails twice
        STT-->>C: Provider error
        C->>S: Speak a local safe handoff
    else Transcript returned
        STT-->>C: "Wait, wrong order."
        C->>S: handle(transcript, channel="voice") → reply audio
    end
    S-->>C: Result for turn 2
    Note over C: Accept only the current turn, discard any late turn-1 result
    C->>P: Play turn 2 reply (2.1-2.9 s after end of speech)
